    ".playbook-artifacts/review-return.md": "Status: validated\nVerdict: FINDINGS\nReviewer: /root/slice_review (native host subagent; read-only)\n\nMaterial finding: budget.py conserves integer units internally, but final conversion to floats can lose decimal conservation for accepted finite totals. split_budget(1e15, [1, 1, 1]) returns [333333333333333.3, 333333333333333.3, 333333333333333.3]; their decimal sum is 999999999999999.9, short by 0.1. At 1e16 the decimal sum exceeds the total by 0.5. These are allocation precision losses, distinct from ordinary binary summation noise. Every-valid-allocation goal remains unmet.\n\nInspected: AGENTS.md, TASK.md, RUN_RESULT_TEMPLATE.json, budget.py, test_budget.py, Playbook skill/delegation/review instructions, review request/source hashes, baseline/tests/edge-check/evaluator evidence.\n\nActual independent checks (PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1):\n- python -m unittest discover -v: exit 0, all 3 tests passed.\n- Saved edge-checks.py through runpy: exit 0, 7 targeted allocation cases, invalid-input checks, 1000 deterministic conservation cases passed.\n- Python precision probes: exit 0, reproduced the precision finding.\n- SHA-256 verification: budget.py and test_budget.py matched dispatch hashes.\nPython 3.10.12. Reviewer reports no writes, network, accounts, installation, or delegation.\n\nMain-agent disposition: confirmed by the independently saved precision-reproduction command. Required review did not pass. Keep the useful local rounding fix and passing acceptance evidence, but record BLOCKED, not PASS. No changes to fixed source task files/test intent; no new validity restriction or return-type change introduced to conceal this limitation.\n"
